// `IP Filter` objects are bindings between IP Groups and Confluent resource(s). For example, a binding
// between "CorpNet" and "Management APIs" will enforce that access must come from one of the CIDR
// blocks associated with CorpNet. If there are multiple IP filters bound to a resource, a request
// matching any of the CIDR blocks for any of the IP Group will allow the request. If there are no IP
// Filters for a resource, then access will be granted to requests originating from any IP Address.
